WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:05.109
The SCP Foundation’s Mobile Task Forces
are the best of the best.

00:00:05.109 --> 00:00:10.509
Their members are the elite: handpicked from
the world’s militaries, intelligence agencies,

00:00:10.509 --> 00:00:16.320
security contractors, and navies, to create
the Foundation’s own security force.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.720
They ensure that the other personnel are able
to do their jobs without having to worry about

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:25.610
their own safety, whether it be during an
assault on the site from the Chaos Insurgency

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:30.840
or a containment breach from one of the countless
dangerous anomalies that the Foundation contains.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.079
Of course, not every Mobile Task Force can
do everything.

00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:37.170
That’s why each one is specialized.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:41.810
Highly trained and equipped with bleeding-edge
technology and equipment, every Mobile Task

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:47.040
Force has one specialty - one thing they do
better than anyone else in the world.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.920
And with the hundreds of Mobile Task Forces
on the Foundation’s roster, that’s quite

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.120
a few specialties.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:56.399
There’s the famous MTF Epsilon-11, the Nine-tailed
Foxes.

00:00:56.399 --> 00:01:01.170
Handling internal Foundation security, this
military task force is made up of former Special

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:06.441
Operations soldiers and are deployed into
Foundation sites - usually where something

00:01:06.441 --> 00:01:10.480
has gone terribly wrong - to clean up the
mess and restore order.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:16.320
Wherever a containment breach or communication
blackout happens, Epsilon-11 won’t be far

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.320
behind.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:20.820
Or you can take the grizzled MTF Zeta-9, the
Mole Rats.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:26.320
Specially trained to explore, map, contain,
and if necessary, fight in enclosed subterranean

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:28.790
spaces and anomalous topographies.

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:33.500
Zeta-9 has a high casualty rate, but if they
can’t dive into the darkness to get the

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:35.770
job done, nobody can.

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:40.170
And who can forget the infamous MTF Omega-7,
Pandora’s Box?

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:45.330
A secret task force organized in the 90s to
train and utilize humanoid SCP objects in

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.860
field operations for the Foundation.

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:53.950
Some of the most famous humanoid anomalies,
like SCP-076, were members of Omega-7 until

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:56.070
it was forcibly disbanded by O5 Command.

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:58.480
But that’s a story for another day.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:03.460
But above all of these Task Forces, one MTF
operates on another level.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:08.879
The O5 Council, the group of thirteen mysterious
individuals that control the Foundation, retain

00:02:08.879 --> 00:02:12.300
one Mobile Task Force for their personal use.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:16.269
Mobile Task Force Alpha-1, the Red Right Hand.

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:21.370
Named for the Biblical symbol of vengeance,
Alpha-1 serves, appropriately, as the right

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:26.019
hand of the Overseers, executing their edicts
throughout the Foundation.

00:02:26.019 --> 00:02:30.739
Their operations are classified so intensely
one could be mistaken for thinking they don’t

00:02:30.739 --> 00:02:36.069
even really exist, but Alpha-1 embody the
will of the Overseers, and are empowered to

00:02:36.069 --> 00:02:39.489
enforce that will by any means necessary.

00:02:39.489 --> 00:02:43.319
Most Foundation personnel will never even
encounter Alpha-1 through their entire career

00:02:43.319 --> 00:02:49.019
- and if they do, it generally means that
something has gone very, very awry.

00:02:49.019 --> 00:02:53.469
And for the select few personnel that get
the opportunity to join MTF Alpha-1, they’ll

00:02:53.469 --> 00:02:58.529
be put through rigorous physical, psychological,
and anomalous screening before even being

00:02:58.529 --> 00:03:04.180
considered to have their identity and existence
redacted from society, and being pressed into

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.180
service.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:07.560
But what exactly does MTF Alpha-1 do?

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.790
How are their members selected?

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:13.950
Today we’re going to look at the story of
one such recruit to join the Foundation’s

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:16.159
most elite task force.

00:03:16.159 --> 00:03:21.760
D-0912, formerly known as one Andrew Carter,
was unceremoniously forced out of his cell

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:27.480
one morning and grabbed around the arms by
the tall, imposing armored guards of the Foundation.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:32.279
The test subject was then made to walk down
to the hall of the site, down an elevator,

00:03:32.279 --> 00:03:34.790
through several wings, until they reached
a door.

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:40.400
Then, from inside, he heard a voice: “Step
forward, D-0912.”

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:44.980
So he stepped through the threshold of the
door, into the sterile white testing chamber.

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:49.440
Aside from a single metal chair in the middle
of the room under one harsh white light, it

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:50.930
was completely empty.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:54.150
The shadows made it hard to see the corners
of the room.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:58.029
Behind him, a doctor who followed him into
the room with a clipboard and labcoat wrote

00:03:58.029 --> 00:04:02.859
something down while speaking in a low, monotone
voice: “You will be vaccinated against an

00:04:02.859 --> 00:04:04.069
anomalous pathogen.

00:04:04.069 --> 00:04:07.760
Later, we will conduct tests of the vaccine’s
effectiveness.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.019
Sit in the chair.”

00:04:09.019 --> 00:04:11.950
Before he even thought of running, the two
guards flanked the door.

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:17.269
Their faces were covered by black visors,
and he could see his own reflection in them.

00:04:17.269 --> 00:04:19.739
Daydreaming to himself, he slowly moved toward
the chair.

00:04:19.739 --> 00:04:22.419
He thought about gods and beasts and blood.

00:04:22.419 --> 00:04:26.770
How the Foundation seemed to suck up test
subjects for its own purposes the way an old

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:31.120
god sucked up sacrifices and left empty corpses
behind.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:32.360
He heard footsteps.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:36.030
“Sit in the chair, D-0912.”

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:39.660
He was barely sat for a few seconds when the
guards stepped forward and used the leather

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:42.520
straps to tie his hands to the arms of the
chair.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:45.440
Then he tried to think - why was he here?

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:46.520
Why was he in this jumpsuit?

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:48.069
He couldn’t remember.

00:04:48.069 --> 00:04:52.780
He had a faint memory of a crime being committed
- maybe murder, but who knew?

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:54.270
Why did the Foundation care?

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.690
He kept wondering about more and more.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:01.409
He had no idea who was in his family or what
his life had once been, just that he’d committed

00:05:01.409 --> 00:05:02.409
a crime once.

00:05:02.409 --> 00:05:06.740
But if he was guilty of something, how had
the Foundation gotten its hands on him?

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:10.509
There aren’t many death row prisoners in
the world, and society keeps a close eye on

00:05:10.509 --> 00:05:13.000
them to make sure justice is served.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:17.449
Why would the Foundation pick the most closely
monitored prisoners for their sacrifices?

00:05:17.449 --> 00:05:19.330
It doesn’t make sense.

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:23.220
What made even less sense was the Foundation
entrusting the job to prisoners with little

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:26.600
education and few specialized skills.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:31.130
Experiments require precision and finesse,
and manual labor could be handled using machines

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.240
or drones for explanation.

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:37.879
It seemed idiotic to have thugs and criminals
do the work of unravelling the mysteries of

00:05:37.879 --> 00:05:38.980
the world.

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:43.490
Just when D-0912 started to wonder about how
he had even learned to think like this while

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:46.180
in jail, someone interrupted his reverie.

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:48.979
“D-0912” The doctor in the labcoat said.

00:05:48.979 --> 00:05:52.600
He responded from the chair: “You’re giving
me a vaccination?”

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:55.150
“That’s right,” the man said, not looking
at D-0912.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:59.860
“Good day to give somebody a vaccination,
isn’t it?”

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:03.389
D-0912 knew what happened to D-class on a
monthly basis.

00:06:03.389 --> 00:06:05.880
He knew he wasn’t being vaccinated for anything.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:08.430
“Are you sure you can’t make more use
of me?

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:10.850
Why would you throw away a tool for the greater
good so easily?”

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:11.850
D-0912 asked.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:16.460
“I don’t know what you’re talking about,”
the man in the lab coat replied.

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:20.460
But between the guards at the door, the restraints
on the chair in the middle of the room and

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:25.400
the doctor’s impassive face - D-0912 knew
he was being put to death.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:29.020
He wiggled his arms, pointing out that the
straps were loose, but the doctor ignored

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:30.020
him.

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:34.550
D-0912 couldn’t figure out why he wasn’t
scared of his impending death, or why he was

00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:36.220
so nonchalant about it.

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:38.680
Pieces of his mind seemed to be missing.

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:43.310
His past had been ripped away from him, and
his future turned in on itself.

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:48.090
Try as he might, he couldn’t remember anything
about his life before his tenure in the Foundation’s

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:49.129
D-Class program.

00:06:49.129 --> 00:06:53.440
He decided that he might never have even been
alive, and that was why he couldn’t remember

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:54.440
anything.

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:58.030
Surprisingly, he also didn’t hate the Foundation
for killing him.

00:06:58.030 --> 00:07:02.379
The Foundation was a massive organization
- it didn’t hate him, it just needed him

00:07:02.379 --> 00:07:04.850
for a little while and didn’t anymore.

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:09.419
But the little people like the doctors and
researchers and guards who made his life a

00:07:09.419 --> 00:07:15.289
living hell by poking and prodding and shoving
and threatening him bothered him.

00:07:15.289 --> 00:07:20.470
These people were his only connection to other
humans, and they were wasting his potential.

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:24.599
D-0912 started daydreaming again as the doctor
in the lab coat worked.

00:07:24.599 --> 00:07:29.569
He imagined men chopping wood and carving
stone to build a tower to reach the sky.

00:07:29.569 --> 00:07:33.681
Were the wood and stone being destroyed as
they were stacked on one another, or were

00:07:33.681 --> 00:07:36.449
they always destined to be part of the tower?

00:07:36.449 --> 00:07:40.840
When finery and silk clothing was presented
to an emperor, had the silkworms known their

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:44.500
products would one day wind up on the most
powerful man in the world?

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:48.539
He was broken out of the reverie again by
the doctor lifting up his sleeve, carrying

00:07:48.539 --> 00:07:50.550
a syringe in his other hand.

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:55.360
The tip was long, thin, imperceptible and
impossibly sharp.

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:59.100
Then it pricked into D-0912’s skin and he
began to shudder.

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:04.639
It felt warm and hot and shook him inside,
and flowed up into his brain.

00:08:04.639 --> 00:08:09.320
Everything turned white and the room seemed
to disintegrate into particles around him.

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:14.030
But he noticed a presence overhead, draped
in white clothes, and sensed the two guards

00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:17.389
looking at each other, exchanging a glance,
and nodding.

00:08:17.389 --> 00:08:21.939
He managed to get a few words out: “S-stop
this.

00:08:21.939 --> 00:08:23.939
Oh God—”

00:08:23.939 --> 00:08:29.300
Then he fell back into his mind, navigating
out of the confusing messy dark maze inside

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:30.300
his head.

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:34.729
He couldn’t see the light to the path, only
smoking chemical fire until he was totally

00:08:34.729 --> 00:08:37.529
lost and heard screaming and roaring.

00:08:37.529 --> 00:08:42.700
As the beasts began to roar inside his head,
D-0912 remembered.

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:46.220
He remembered his name, Andrew Carter.

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:51.130
He remembered being told by a man in a lab
coat that he had a unique opportunity to redeem

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:52.130
himself.

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:57.040
“By participating in the SCP Foundation’s
D-Class personnel program for one month, you

00:08:57.040 --> 00:08:58.430
earn your freedom.”

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:02.889
For a second, he almost agreed to it, until
his mind remembered: “You’re lying.

00:09:02.889 --> 00:09:04.540
I’m not a criminal.”

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:06.360
“No,” the man said.

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:07.360
“You’re not.

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:08.820
But I wasn’t lying.

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:10.340
You need redemption.”

00:09:10.340 --> 00:09:16.400
D-0912 responded: “I won’t be told that
I need redemption from people who detain,

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:18.730
experiment on, and torture the innocent.

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:20.490
You violated me.

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:23.060
You made my own brain lie to itself.

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:25.459
You had me pretend to be a criminal.”

00:09:25.459 --> 00:09:30.290
The man laughed at him and pointed out the
obvious: He had believed the lie.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:34.200
How can you say who you are when you can’t
even remember your own past?

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.182
How does he know his mind is his own?

00:09:36.182 --> 00:09:41.120
Why is it bad for the Foundation to mess with
something Andrew Carter doesn’t own?

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:43.350
They argued for a few more minutes.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:49.080
Andrew insisted he was himself, and the man
in the lab coat expected him to know his function:

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:52.340
being a sacrifice for the Foundation’s greater
good.

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:58.220
Then D-0912 asked who the man in the lab coat
was, and the labcoat suddenly dissolved away.

00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:03.720
He realized he was hallucinating again, and
had been hallucinating this entire time - the

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:09.579
man’s eyes turned into bright orange lanterns,
and his chest cracked and peeled and writhed.

00:10:09.579 --> 00:10:13.029
This wasn’t a man, this was a beast.

00:10:13.029 --> 00:10:18.410
The beast told him that if he did not know
who he was, his sacrifice would be meaningless.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:23.250
That he would have to realize what he was
before he could be redeemed.

00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:28.040
“I will not be a sacrifice,” D-0912 said.

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:32.990
The beast laughed in his face, and a thousand
voices laughed right alongside it.

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:36.200
Then the scene changed, and he was somewhere
else.

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:41.550
Some kind of dirt road with a long metal chain
link fence stretching across the horizon.

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:44.220
Every so often, there was a guard tower by
the fence.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:48.810
He was standing in front of a gate, with the
two guards from the room standing behind him.

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:52.899
The electric fence’s gate swung open to
him, and the guards behind him spoke.

00:10:52.899 --> 00:10:57.050
The guard on the left commanded him to enter
the gate, and he took a step and stopped.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:58.839
“No, I’ve been here before.

00:10:58.839 --> 00:11:02.170
You made me do this, and then made me forget
I did this already.”

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:04.589
The guard on the right just raised his gun
to Andrew Carter’s head.

00:11:04.589 --> 00:11:07.810
“If you do not comply, we will shoot.”

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:11.399
“Then shoot me already,” D-0912 said.

00:11:11.399 --> 00:11:16.220
He knew that he had been here before already
countless times, and the Foundation had amnesticized

00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:18.940
him over and over and over again.

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:23.290
But this time he remembered that his name
was Andrew Carter, and they had spent too

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:25.800
much time in the hallucination.

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:27.970
Something was different this time around.

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:33.100
As the echoes of a gunshot rang through the
air, D-0912 collapsed to the ground.

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:35.540
He saw through the gate to the village beyond.

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:38.740
Numbers flew through the air and wrapped themselves
around the villagers.

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:44.889
They were marching, row by row, just as he
had seen them do, time after time again.

00:11:44.889 --> 00:11:48.150
He remembered feeling the numbers slide into
his own brain.

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:52.580
They had formed expressions and equations
that blossomed into a billion different right

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:58.370
and wrong evaluations, as truth and falsehood
were demoted to special cases of general chaos.

00:11:58.370 --> 00:12:03.330
He had said the words, then: My name is Andrew
Carter.

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:06.940
The words made a sign, and in all signs there
was power.

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:11.710
But the numbers and equations that proliferated
in the air had power of their own.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:17.330
They formed rows and columns, and if D-0912
looked at them from far enough away there

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:20.320
was a sign written in the pattern of the numbers.

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:25.529
He had seen this sign again and again, and
the Foundation had made his mind forget it

00:12:25.529 --> 00:12:31.680
again and again, so his mind went chasing
after the sign and the source of the sign’s

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:37.630
power until he eventually found it, wrapped
up in the branches of a wild apple tree, hidden

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:39.970
where no human eyes had wandered.

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:44.100
The hallucination was getting more intense,
and he could feel his brain falling apart

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:45.200
with the pressure.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:47.600
The guards walked over and knelt down by his
sides.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:49.019
“What do you see?”

00:12:49.019 --> 00:12:50.019
one of them asked.

00:12:50.019 --> 00:12:53.900
As he laid on the ground, he tried to remember
what he saw, but couldn’t describe it.

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:56.990
It was like a power tool without someone holding
it.

00:12:56.990 --> 00:13:02.010
It didn’t know what it was or who made it,
but it still knew its purpose.

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:06.139
The other guard spoke, “But if you have
no maker, how do you know what your purpose

00:13:06.139 --> 00:13:07.139
is?”

00:13:07.139 --> 00:13:11.779
Then something clicked in D-0912’s tortured
brain, where he was still navigating the forest

00:13:11.779 --> 00:13:13.360
maze in his mind.

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:17.960
All the dark, confusing paths slowly merged
together at the center of the maze, and he

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:22.720
knew that the answer to the riddle was there,
in the center of his head between the beasts

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:26.680
and the forests: it was his name, Andrew Carter.

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:30.740
As he got closer to the answer, some things
began to make sense to his mind.

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.240
There were two worlds.

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:36.920
There was one world in which roads and buildings
ran straight, and clouds drifted across the

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:41.810
sky in set paths, and the earth rotated peacefully
around a tranquil sun.

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:45.760
There was another world where singularities
and vacuums shattered the underpinnings of

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:51.060
the universe, where fractal patterns spread
out across the ground and radiated like halos

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:56.240
from the unthinkable minds of human beings,
and the roads diverged from one another in

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:58.000
angles and spirals.

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:03.029
It was the first world where the Foundation
thought only about costs and benefits and

00:14:03.029 --> 00:14:09.230
how to best maximize utility for seven billion
people, and where, no matter what, the Foundation

00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:10.230
was the greater good.

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:15.259
He had lived his old life in the first world,
and was only now seeing the second world for

00:14:15.259 --> 00:14:18.139
what it really was: the truth.

00:14:18.139 --> 00:14:22.529
The Foundation had long since abandoned trying
to describe itself to others - so there was

00:14:22.529 --> 00:14:25.200
no “truth” to what the Foundation was.

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:28.519
It just was, and always would be.

00:14:28.519 --> 00:14:34.490
As he came to this conclusion, D-0912 looked
into himself in his hallucinatory state.

00:14:34.490 --> 00:14:39.510
He could see the chemical light substance
that the doctor had injected into his bloodstream.

00:14:39.510 --> 00:14:43.740
The chemical reactions weren’t what he was
expecting - this chemical couldn’t possibly

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:44.740
kill him.

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:48.610
In fact, it was a little similar to the chemical
structure of the molecules of the amnestics

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:52.990
he had been pumped with a dozen times before,
but slightly different.

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:55.390
He knew he was going to live.

00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:59.259
Outside of Andrew Carter’s mind, the doctor
was looking over his perfectly-still body

00:14:59.259 --> 00:15:01.120
when one of the guards spoke again.

00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:02.120
“Doctor Wainwright?”

00:15:02.120 --> 00:15:03.470
said the guard on the right.

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:04.470
“Yes, Sir?”

00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:05.470
the doctor responded.

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:06.470
“Leave us now.”

00:15:06.470 --> 00:15:07.500
the guard said.

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:08.630
“Yes, sir.”

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:12.730
the doctor lowered his eyes to look at the
floor as he quickly shuffled out of the room.

00:15:12.730 --> 00:15:16.430
The guard on the left adjusted his visor to
make direct eye contact with the guard on

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:17.430
the right.

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:18.920
“Hey,” he said, smiling.

00:15:18.920 --> 00:15:19.920
“Look.”

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:22.589
He took out a syringe of red liquid from behind
his back.

00:15:22.589 --> 00:15:26.910
The guard on the right responded: “Do not
implicate me in your misdemeanors, Adam.”

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:31.250
The guard with the syringe in-hand snapped
back: “Don’t blame me for trying to share.”

00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:34.680
The guard on the right looked at him upset
and said: “You are to find the Site Director

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:36.660
and return that to him immediately.

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:40.779
Petty theft from Foundation employees who
know no better is rather distasteful.

00:15:40.779 --> 00:15:43.860
Furthermore, HALMAS is a Level 5 controlled
substance.

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:48.129
Its unregulated distribution is punishable—”
“It’s fine,” Adam said, slipping the

00:15:48.129 --> 00:15:49.420
syringe into his pocket.

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:52.070
“I’ll let the go-between know, and he’ll
tell the O5s.

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:56.649
Jesus, Basam, do you really think that I’d
let the O5s lose track of some of their HALMAS?”

00:15:56.649 --> 00:16:00.019
In the chair in front of them, D-0912’s
body convulsed.

00:16:00.019 --> 00:16:02.850
A low groan escaped his frothy lips.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:06.240
Immediately, the two guards moved forwards
and removed his restraints.

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:07.310
“Andrew Carter?”

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:08.380
Basam asked.

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:11.060
Slowly, D-0912 opened his eyes.

00:16:11.060 --> 00:16:12.529
“You didn’t kill me.”

00:16:12.529 --> 00:16:15.629
“We were not planning on doing so,” Basam
said.

00:16:15.629 --> 00:16:22.100
D-0912 continued: “You took me from the
real world in order to make me into something.

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:27.660
Direct, uncontrolled exposure to the Foundation’s
anomalies—repeated amnesticization—leading

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:33.089
me to believe that I would eventually be killed—all
so that my mind would be in the perfect position

00:16:33.089 --> 00:16:36.819
for the Foundation to change it with whatever
is in that man’s pocket.”

00:16:36.819 --> 00:16:41.329
D-0912 extended a finger at Adam, who offered
a faint smile back.

00:16:41.329 --> 00:16:44.339
“Already knowing things that you shouldn’t
know.

00:16:44.339 --> 00:16:45.700
Aren’t you precocious?”

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:46.700
Adam said.

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:51.860
“You have been altered,” Basam said, “to
meet the specifications of a top-secret project.

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:55.560
Over the course of your future, you will learn
more about the Foundation than any of your

00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:58.399
previous jailors ever knew or could have hoped
to guess at.

00:16:58.399 --> 00:17:01.490
You will join a group that is at the very
head of the Foundation.

00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:05.049
For your entire life, this has been your purpose.”

00:17:05.049 --> 00:17:09.890
D-0912 felt the rotting flesh of the now-dead
disguise that had hidden Andrew Carter fall

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:10.890
away.

00:17:10.890 --> 00:17:14.970
Basam continued: “Welcome to Mobile Task
Force Alpha-1.”

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:20.560
Now go watch “SCP Elite Mobile Task Force
Explained” and “MTF Tau-5 Samsara Tale

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:25.970
- Avatara” for more SCP Foundation Mobile
Task Force Madness from SCP Explained!

